WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
On a 1080×1080 square canvas, select the Pen tool.

00:05.000 --> 00:15.000
Tap eight points around the sun, then tap the starting point to close the path.

00:15.000 --> 00:20.000
Open the object appearance settings and turn off the sun’s stroke.

00:20.000 --> 00:30.000
Choose Fill in the saved palette and set the sun to amber.

00:30.000 --> 00:39.000
Tap out a triangle below and to the left of the sun, then close the first mountain.

00:39.000 --> 00:49.500
Fill the main peak blue, retaining its overlap with the sun.

00:49.500 --> 01:00.000
Add a lower mountain on the right, aligning the bases of both peaks.

01:00.000 --> 01:07.000
Turn off the second mountain’s stroke so the filled shape defines its outline.

01:07.000 --> 01:17.000
Fill the second peak purple to create two overlapping mountain silhouettes.

01:17.000 --> 01:27.000
Open Export & Share and choose PNG image.

01:27.000 --> 01:31.000
Use the complete 1080×1080 canvas with a white background.

01:31.000 --> 01:39.000
Tap Export PNG and wait for the system share sheet.

01:39.000 --> 01:43.000
The PNG is ready. Save it to Files from the share sheet.

01:43.000 --> 01:49.500
Finished: three solid-color shapes form a simple mountain sunset.
